BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:state-pte-georgia-2025-03-17@ustaxcalendar.com
DTSTAMP:20260924T122623Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20250317
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20250318
SUMMARY:Georgia: Form 700 due
DESCRIPTION:Georgia partnership return (also used for S-corps) due the 15th
  day of the 3rd month after year-end. Correction (this rebuild session): th
 e cited source states the general rule (15th day of the 3rd month) without 
 addressing the 2026-specific weekend interaction - March 15\, 2026 is a Sun
 day. Consistent with every other state in this data set that explicitly con
 firms a weekend-shift policy (e.g. Massachusetts\, New York\, Vermont\, Del
 aware\, Montana\, Oregon all confirm shifting to March 16\, 2026)\, and wit
 h the near-universal US government-deadline convention of shifting to the n
 ext business day\, this entry's date_2026 was corrected from an unshifted M
 arch 15\, 2026 to March 16\, 2026. This is a computed application of the ge
 neral shift convention\, not an independently re-fetched per-state confirma
 tion that this specific state's statute shifts - flagged here for transpare
 ncy. | Georgia partnership return (also used for S-corps) due the 15th day 
 of the 3rd month after year-end. If a federal extension (Form 7004) is file
 d by the original due date\, Georgia grants an additional 6 months automati
 cally. Correction (this rebuild session): the cited source states the gener
 al rule (15th day of the 3rd month) without addressing the 2026-specific we
 ekend interaction - March 15\, 2026 is a Sunday. Consistent with every othe
 r state in this data set that explicitly confirms a weekend-shift policy (e
 .g. Massachusetts\, New York\, Vermont\, Delaware\, Montana\, Oregon all co
 nfirm shifting to March 16\, 2026)\, and with the near-universal US governm
 ent-deadline convention of shifting to the next business day\, this entry's
  date_2026 was corrected from an unshifted March 15\, 2026 to March 16\, 20
 26. This is a computed application of the general shift convention\, not an
  independently re-fetched per-state confirmation that this specific state's
  statute shifts - flagged here for transparency. | Authority: Georgia Depar
 tment of Revenue\, direct fetch this session: "Partnership income tax retur
 ns are due on or before the 15th day of the third month following the close
  of the taxable year" and "If you have... filed a Federal extension (Form 7
 004) by the original due date... you will be granted an additional 6 months
  to file." | Source: https://dor.georgia.gov/partnership-due-dates | This d
 ate is computed from a recurrence rule and may not reflect a later-announce
 d change\; confirm against the cited source before relying on it.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
