UID:state-pte-georgia-2032-09-15-ext@ustaxcalendar.com
DTSTAMP:20260924T122623Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20320915
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20320916
SUMMARY:Georgia: Form 700 extended due date
DESCRIPTION:Extended due date\, via If a federal extension (Form 7004) is f
 iled by the original due date\, Georgia grants an additional 6 months autom
 atically.. | Georgia partnership return (also used for S-corps) due the 15t
 h day of the 3rd month after year-end. If a federal extension (Form 7004) i
 s filed by the original due date\, Georgia grants an additional 6 months au
 tomatically. Correction (this rebuild session): the cited source states the
  general rule (15th day of the 3rd month) without addressing the 2026-speci
 fic weekend interaction - March 15\, 2026 is a Sunday. Consistent with ever
 y other state in this data set that explicitly confirms a weekend-shift pol
 icy (e.g. Massachusetts\, New York\, Vermont\, Delaware\, Montana\, Oregon 
 all confirm shifting to March 16\, 2026)\, and with the near-universal US g
 overnment-deadline convention of shifting to the next business day\, this e
 ntry's date_2026 was corrected from an unshifted March 15\, 2026 to March 1
 6\, 2026. This is a computed application of the general shift convention\, 
 not an independently re-fetched per-state confirmation that this specific s
 tate's statute shifts - flagged here for transparency. | Authority: Georgia
  Department of Revenue\, direct fetch this session: "Partnership income tax
  returns are due on or before the 15th day of the third month following the
  close of the taxable year" and "If you have... filed a Federal extension (
 Form 7004) by the original due date... you will be granted an additional 6 
 months to file." | Source: https://dor.georgia.gov/partnership-due-dates | 
 This date is computed from a recurrence rule and may not reflect a later-an
 nounced change\; confirm against the cited source before relying on it.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
